1
00:00:00,328 --> 00:00:01,358
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,358 --> 00:00:02,398
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,398 --> 00:00:03,398
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:04,728 --> 00:00:06,398
(Episode 10)

5
00:00:42,098 --> 00:00:43,898
Gyu Rim. Han Gyu Rim.

6
00:00:44,238 --> 00:00:45,338
Gyu Rim.

7
00:00:52,148 --> 00:00:53,208
What has gotten into you?

8
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:55,378
Where did you drink so much?

9
00:00:55,618 --> 00:00:57,218
You can't even handle your alcohol.

10
00:01:00,848 --> 00:01:01,958
Who are you?

11
00:01:03,558 --> 00:01:04,688
Do I know you?

12
00:01:06,628 --> 00:01:07,658
You've got to be kidding me.

13
00:01:14,998 --> 00:01:15,998
Come on, try again.

14
00:01:19,208 --> 00:01:20,238
Get up.

15
00:01:28,118 --> 00:01:30,918
You look a lot like Kim Mu Jin.

16
00:01:34,918 --> 00:01:38,888
But you're not as good-looking as Kim Mu Jin.

17
00:01:40,358 --> 00:01:41,358
Get up.

18
00:01:44,728 --> 00:01:47,168
Thank you. You can go now.

19
00:02:40,088 --> 00:02:41,818
Where's my phone?

20
00:02:45,228 --> 00:02:46,828
What do I do? Oh my.

21
00:02:47,288 --> 00:02:49,528
Your phone is in your hand.

22
00:02:49,858 --> 00:02:51,868
Thank you.

23
00:02:58,968 --> 00:02:59,968
Hello.

24
00:02:59,968 --> 00:03:02,138
Where are you? Are you still at the bar?

25
00:03:08,948 --> 00:03:10,878
When Mom left home,

26
00:03:15,058 --> 00:03:17,318
I said I would go with her.

27
00:03:19,928 --> 00:03:21,228
She said I couldn't.

28
00:03:22,998 --> 00:03:24,198
Because I'm the eldest daughter.

29
00:03:24,928 --> 00:03:25,928
What are you talking about?

30
00:03:26,028 --> 00:03:27,698
Are you still at the bar?

31
00:03:27,698 --> 00:03:29,838
"Gyu Rim, since you're the eldest,"

32
00:03:31,298 --> 00:03:34,268
"you have to take good care of your younger siblings."

33
00:03:40,948 --> 00:03:44,048
She said I had to be their mom.

34
00:03:45,318 --> 00:03:47,218
She said I should endure things even when they're hard...

35
00:03:48,258 --> 00:03:49,958
and give in even when it's unfair.

36
00:03:51,288 --> 00:03:53,528
She said to compromise and be understanding.

37
00:03:54,788 --> 00:03:56,198
Because I'm the eldest daughter.

38
00:03:57,458 --> 00:03:58,498
The eldest daughter...

39
00:03:59,898 --> 00:04:01,468
is supposed to do all that.

40
00:04:02,298 --> 00:04:04,168
What is this? So annoying.

41
00:04:04,238 --> 00:04:05,738
If you're just going to drunk-ramble, I'm hanging up.

42
00:04:06,608 --> 00:04:08,278
Don't hang up.

43
00:04:09,138 --> 00:04:10,478
Don't hang up.

44
00:04:12,448 --> 00:04:14,608
Don't hang up and listen, you brat.

45
00:04:17,618 --> 00:04:19,488
I'm the eldest daughter, after all.

46
00:04:20,888 --> 00:04:23,058
So I did everything Mom told me to.

47
00:04:24,418 --> 00:04:25,988
I endured the hardships...

48
00:04:26,758 --> 00:04:28,258
gave in even when it was unfair,

49
00:04:30,858 --> 00:04:33,128
and couldn't do a single thing I wanted to.

50
00:04:35,298 --> 00:04:36,698
I gave up on...

51
00:04:38,938 --> 00:04:40,108
the man I loved.

52
00:04:41,368 --> 00:04:43,208
That's how I've lived my life.

53
00:04:43,678 --> 00:04:45,448
Why are you yelling at me?

54
00:04:45,508 --> 00:04:47,148
If you feel so wronged, take it up with Mom.

55
00:04:47,208 --> 00:04:48,748
She's super rich now.

56
00:04:49,118 --> 00:04:50,978
Tell her you lived like an idiot listening to her,

57
00:04:51,048 --> 00:04:53,188
tell her to buy you an apartment then.

58
00:04:53,318 --> 00:04:54,788
Hey, you idiot.

59
00:04:55,558 --> 00:04:57,958
That's not what I mean.

60
00:04:58,188 --> 00:05:00,958
You don't get it. This is so frustrating.

61
00:05:02,258 --> 00:05:03,458
I'm hanging up.

62
00:05:46,008 --> 00:05:47,738
Thank you.

63
00:06:03,818 --> 00:06:06,028
This is so weird.

64
00:06:07,688 --> 00:06:08,698
What is?

65
00:06:11,298 --> 00:06:15,268
I keep seeing you as Kim Mu Jin.

66
00:06:17,798 --> 00:06:20,608
For all you know, I could be Kim Mu Jin.

67
00:06:25,478 --> 00:06:26,708
Come on.

68
00:06:27,478 --> 00:06:30,778
You're saying Kim Mu Jin is this ugly?

69
00:06:31,178 --> 00:06:33,988
That's ridiculous.

70
00:06:35,418 --> 00:06:37,488
Why are you insulting my looks?

71
00:06:38,388 --> 00:06:41,088
How handsome can Kim Mu Jin be anyway?

72
00:06:44,758 --> 00:06:46,298
He's very handsome.

73
00:06:47,668 --> 00:06:49,238
Kim Mu Jin is...

74
00:06:50,238 --> 00:06:52,838
incredibly...

75
00:06:56,308 --> 00:06:57,838
handsome.

76
00:07:04,448 --> 00:07:06,548
Why did you break up with...

77
00:07:07,948 --> 00:07:09,258
that incredibly handsome man?

78
00:07:13,128 --> 00:07:14,958
That we broke up...

79
00:07:16,198 --> 00:07:17,658
How did he know?

80
00:07:20,898 --> 00:07:22,198
Because you broke up.

81
00:07:22,968 --> 00:07:23,968
That's why you're out here all alone,

82
00:07:24,038 --> 00:07:25,638
drinking your sorrows away, right?

83
00:08:05,248 --> 00:08:06,648
What are you doing? You can't just cross like that.

84
00:08:06,708 --> 00:08:08,008
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

85
00:08:13,448 --> 00:08:15,158
Why are you talking to me so informally?

86
00:08:16,888 --> 00:08:17,918
Am I?

87
00:08:18,958 --> 00:08:19,988
When?

88
00:08:20,188 --> 00:08:23,698
Why do you keep following me?

89
00:08:27,268 --> 00:08:28,598
I'm not following you.

90
00:08:29,538 --> 00:08:31,168
I'm just going my own way.

91
00:08:35,068 --> 00:08:38,548
Did that incredibly handsome Kim Mu Jin...

92
00:08:40,278 --> 00:08:41,778
give you a hard time?

93
00:08:46,688 --> 00:08:47,918
He cheated on you, didn't he?

94
00:08:51,288 --> 00:08:54,028
Did he hit you? Was it dating violence?

95
00:08:55,128 --> 00:08:56,728
Darn it.

96
00:08:57,028 --> 00:08:59,328
My Mu Jin is not that kind of person.

97
00:09:00,068 --> 00:09:01,698
You don't know anything about him.

98
00:09:02,968 --> 00:09:04,638
Still, there must have been some problem.

99
00:09:05,368 --> 00:09:06,838
That's why you two broke up.

100
00:09:08,038 --> 00:09:11,878
Just think of this as a safe space and go ahead and vent all you want.

101
00:09:14,978 --> 00:09:16,048
Go on.

102
00:09:16,178 --> 00:09:18,048
It's not like I'm going to tell anyone.

103
00:09:18,788 --> 00:09:20,148
We'll probably never...

104
00:09:23,088 --> 00:09:24,758
see each other again anyway.

105
00:09:25,988 --> 00:09:27,788
Go on, just badmouth that jerk.

106
00:09:31,998 --> 00:09:33,698
How dare you call Mu Jin a jerk?

107
00:09:35,068 --> 00:09:36,768
Don't you dare talk about him like that.

108
00:09:38,908 --> 00:09:41,838
He's not someone you can just talk trash about.

109
00:09:44,978 --> 00:09:46,848
He's a wonderful person.

110
00:09:49,278 --> 00:09:50,648
If he's such a great guy,

111
00:09:51,818 --> 00:09:53,818
why would he let a woman like you go?

112
00:09:54,718 --> 00:09:58,218
How stupid, foolish and pathetic would he have to be?

113
00:09:59,488 --> 00:10:01,388
I was the one who ran away.

114
00:10:03,428 --> 00:10:05,128
Because I'm stupid,

115
00:10:05,628 --> 00:10:07,328
because I'm foolish,

116
00:10:08,198 --> 00:10:09,898
and because I'm pathetic.

117
00:10:12,968 --> 00:10:15,068
That's why I ran away.

118
00:10:16,508 --> 00:10:17,738
Why would you run away?

119
00:10:18,908 --> 00:10:19,908
If he was such a wonderful person,

120
00:10:19,908 --> 00:10:21,508
you should have held on to him no matter what.

121
00:10:22,248 --> 00:10:24,948
You should never have given up on him, no matter what.

122
00:10:25,548 --> 00:10:28,188
Why did you run away? It's driving me crazy.

123
00:10:34,888 --> 00:10:36,858
Why is it driving you crazy?

124
00:10:43,298 --> 00:10:44,568
You're...

125
00:10:46,038 --> 00:10:47,468
You're Kim Mu Jin, aren't you?

126
00:11:07,788 --> 00:11:10,358
No, that can't be right.

127
00:11:12,528 --> 00:11:15,338
You're way uglier than Kim Mu Jin.

128
00:11:20,868 --> 00:11:22,438
Green light.

129
00:11:22,908 --> 00:11:24,038
The light is green.

130
00:11:28,918 --> 00:11:30,278
Don't follow me.

131
00:11:32,288 --> 00:11:33,688
Because of you,

132
00:11:34,848 --> 00:11:37,388
I miss Kim Mu Jin like crazy now.

133
00:12:20,628 --> 00:12:21,998
Which way do I go?

134
00:12:23,568 --> 00:12:25,268
Which way is my house?

135
00:12:27,968 --> 00:12:29,108
I think I've lost my mind.

136
00:12:30,378 --> 00:12:32,848
Seriously, why did I drink so much?

137
00:12:35,278 --> 00:12:36,378
Get a grip, Han Gyu Rim.

138
00:12:37,018 --> 00:12:38,018
It's okay.

139
00:12:38,018 --> 00:12:39,018
Gyu Rim.

140
00:12:45,258 --> 00:12:46,358
Who are you?

141
00:12:49,528 --> 00:12:51,458
You look so familiar.

142
00:12:52,168 --> 00:12:54,228
Hey, it's me, Gyu Seo.

143
00:12:55,168 --> 00:12:56,998
I had a hunch it was you.

144
00:12:57,498 --> 00:12:58,768
You're Gyu Seo?

145
00:13:00,138 --> 00:13:01,138
Hey.

146
00:13:02,838 --> 00:13:04,208
Don't you lie to me.

147
00:13:05,038 --> 00:13:06,148
You have three eyes, don't you?

148
00:13:06,548 --> 00:13:09,618
My Gyu Seo has two eyes.

149
00:13:12,718 --> 00:13:16,458
But I've seen so many people who look alike today.

150
00:13:17,218 --> 00:13:18,958
How much did you drink?

151
00:13:19,658 --> 00:13:21,288
Let's just get you home, okay?

152
00:13:21,488 --> 00:13:22,498
We can talk when we get home.

153
00:13:29,668 --> 00:13:32,208
Looking at your hand, it really is my Gyu Seo's.

154
00:13:32,668 --> 00:13:34,138
When you were little,

155
00:13:34,138 --> 00:13:35,408
you always held my hand just like this. Right?

156
00:13:35,578 --> 00:13:37,108
I'm glad you at least recognised my hand.

157
00:13:46,088 --> 00:13:47,088
Why?

158
00:13:48,188 --> 00:13:49,818
No, it's nothing.

159
00:13:52,018 --> 00:13:53,028
Let's go.

160
00:13:54,758 --> 00:13:55,828
Walk slowly.

161
00:13:57,128 --> 00:13:58,198
I'm so tired.

162
00:14:00,898 --> 00:14:02,168
What's so funny?

163
00:14:02,898 --> 00:14:03,898
I don't know.

164
00:14:26,158 --> 00:14:29,358
For her to get that blackout drunk,

165
00:14:29,698 --> 00:14:33,028
means something beyond her control...

166
00:14:33,098 --> 00:14:35,498
and something huge must have happened.

167
00:14:36,368 --> 00:14:38,138
What does "blackout drunk" mean?

168
00:14:38,468 --> 00:14:39,508
Totally hammered...

169
00:14:40,968 --> 00:14:41,968
You explain it.

170
00:14:42,908 --> 00:14:46,078
It means you're completely out of your mind.

171
00:14:47,308 --> 00:14:48,648
Dad, did you make her mad?

172
00:14:49,648 --> 00:14:52,078
What? Am I everyone's punching bag?

173
00:14:52,618 --> 00:14:53,848
Hey, don't you remember that time...

174
00:14:53,918 --> 00:14:55,248
you made your sister lose her temper?

175
00:14:55,318 --> 00:14:58,058
- She drank herself sick, remember? - When did I do that?

176
00:14:58,058 --> 00:14:59,658
When you were in middle school,

177
00:14:59,728 --> 00:15:01,658
you hung out with a bad crowd and ran away.

178
00:15:01,728 --> 00:15:03,558
- I was the one who ran away. - Oh, really?

179
00:15:03,558 --> 00:15:05,158
She said she wasn't going to high school,

180
00:15:05,158 --> 00:15:07,328
so Gyu Rim once drank herself into the hospital.

181
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:09,568
Gyu Rim was hospitalized because of me?

182
00:15:09,668 --> 00:15:10,898
Yes, she was.

183
00:15:11,598 --> 00:15:14,708
And of all things, she drank Dad's 90-proof Chinese liquor.

184
00:15:15,878 --> 00:15:17,138
See?

185
00:15:17,278 --> 00:15:19,648
It all comes out if you dig a little.

186
00:15:20,408 --> 00:15:21,678
And you too, Gyu Oh.

187
00:15:21,748 --> 00:15:24,048
You were always getting into all sorts of fights,

188
00:15:24,118 --> 00:15:26,588
and you made your sister a nervous wreck.

189
00:15:26,788 --> 00:15:27,788
If you collected all the soju bottles...

190
00:15:27,848 --> 00:15:29,088
Gyu Rim drank because of you,

191
00:15:29,558 --> 00:15:30,758
you could build a mountain this high.

192
00:15:31,088 --> 00:15:32,628
That's why I'm keeping my mouth shut.

193
00:15:32,888 --> 00:15:33,988
Keep it shut.

194
00:15:35,158 --> 00:15:40,268
But Gyu Rim's problem is she only drinks hard liquor.

195
00:15:41,268 --> 00:15:43,338
Hey, she must eat food with her drinks and pace yourself.

196
00:15:43,398 --> 00:15:44,698
- And pace herself... - Seriously.

197
00:15:44,768 --> 00:15:46,108
This punk. Pace yourself...

198
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:48,638
You have to know how to pace yourself.

199
00:15:48,978 --> 00:15:51,208
What is this? What kind of family is this?

200
00:15:51,608 --> 00:15:52,648
This is just how we are.

201
00:15:55,948 --> 00:15:58,078
Anyone would think this was Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs.

202
00:15:58,678 --> 00:15:59,918
Gyu Rim's nemesis is this one here.

203
00:15:59,988 --> 00:16:01,948
You're tied for first place.

204
00:16:01,948 --> 00:16:03,118
What are you talking about?

205
00:16:03,888 --> 00:16:05,688
Is she still not awake? It's so loud in here.

206
00:16:06,488 --> 00:16:08,788
No wonder. She was drinking soju like it was water.

207
00:16:08,928 --> 00:16:10,128
You were drinking with her?

208
00:16:10,458 --> 00:16:11,458
What?

209
00:16:11,528 --> 00:16:13,468
You were drinking with her and just left her there?

210
00:16:13,668 --> 00:16:15,028
What do you mean, left her?

211
00:16:15,268 --> 00:16:16,598
She was the one who wanted to drink,

212
00:16:16,668 --> 00:16:18,198
and I had to leave early because I had something to do.

213
00:16:18,438 --> 00:16:19,668
Like that would happen.

214
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:21,968
You're busted.

215
00:16:22,278 --> 00:16:24,108
The culprit is Han Gyu Young.

216
00:16:26,048 --> 00:16:27,848
- I need to talk to you. - Why? I didn't do anything wrong.

217
00:16:27,908 --> 00:16:29,678
- Come on, get out here. - Darn it.

218
00:16:35,388 --> 00:16:36,988
That hurts. Let go of me.

219
00:16:37,418 --> 00:16:38,418
Come on.

220
00:16:39,058 --> 00:16:40,658
You left a bruise.

221
00:16:40,858 --> 00:16:43,158
You jerk. My wedding is soon.

222
00:16:43,228 --> 00:16:44,758
Will you take responsibility if you break my wrist?

223
00:16:45,598 --> 00:16:46,968
Why was Gyu Rim drinking?

224
00:16:47,568 --> 00:16:50,298
Why are you asking me? Go wake Han Gyu Rim up and ask her.

225
00:16:50,798 --> 00:16:52,068
I'm asking you why she was drinking.

226
00:16:52,438 --> 00:16:54,238
Oh, this is driving me crazy.

227
00:16:55,408 --> 00:16:56,978
Her life is a mess, but her younger sister...

228
00:16:57,038 --> 00:16:59,908
is marrying into a good family. I guess she's just green with envy.

229
00:17:00,048 --> 00:17:01,278
Do you hear yourself?

230
00:17:01,348 --> 00:17:03,448
It's a fact. I'm telling you, it's because she's jealous.

231
00:17:03,578 --> 00:17:04,618
Do you think she's like you?

232
00:17:05,018 --> 00:17:06,688
She's human, isn't she? She's a woman.

233
00:17:06,748 --> 00:17:08,518
It's only natural for her to be jealous.

234
00:17:08,958 --> 00:17:11,718
You've dated so many women, yet you still don't understand them?

235
00:17:12,388 --> 00:17:14,428
- Hey. - She was so jealous of me

236
00:17:14,428 --> 00:17:17,128
that she drank herself into a stupor. Satisfied?

237
00:17:19,228 --> 00:17:21,628
Gyu Rim gave up on college because of you.

238
00:17:22,068 --> 00:17:23,168
To send you to med school,

239
00:17:23,238 --> 00:17:24,768
she gave up on her own dream.

240
00:17:25,198 --> 00:17:26,408
What dream? Han Gyu Rim never had one.

241
00:17:26,408 --> 00:17:27,708
She doesn't have any dreams.

242
00:17:27,808 --> 00:17:29,608
Besides, I was the better student.

243
00:17:29,838 --> 00:17:32,778
If only one person in our poor family could go to college,

244
00:17:33,548 --> 00:17:34,608
then it was right for me to go.

245
00:17:36,348 --> 00:17:37,378
Are you even human?

246
00:18:11,018 --> 00:18:12,018
Mom.

247
00:18:12,788 --> 00:18:13,918
Why are you crying?

248
00:18:16,618 --> 00:18:17,988
Did you have a bad dream?

249
00:18:23,328 --> 00:18:24,398
Are you thirsty?

250
00:18:25,128 --> 00:18:26,298
Should I get you some water?

251
00:18:28,768 --> 00:18:29,868
Do you feel like you're going to throw up?

252
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:31,768
Should I get you some medicine?

253
00:18:39,148 --> 00:18:40,348
I don't need medicine.

254
00:18:41,908 --> 00:18:43,748
Just give Mom a hug, Gyeol.

255
00:18:44,778 --> 00:18:45,788
What?

256
00:18:46,048 --> 00:18:47,148
Come here, my sweet boy.

257
00:18:54,428 --> 00:18:55,458
I'm sorry...

258
00:18:56,758 --> 00:18:58,458
for making you worry.

259
00:18:59,368 --> 00:19:00,828
I'm so sorry, sweetie.

260
00:19:02,098 --> 00:19:03,098
Never again.

261
00:19:04,068 --> 00:19:07,238
This will never happen again. I'm sorry, Gyeol.

262
00:19:07,908 --> 00:19:09,338
It's okay, Mom.

263
00:19:09,738 --> 00:19:10,808
It's okay.

264
00:19:28,628 --> 00:19:30,498
Don't hang up and listen, you brat.

265
00:19:30,958 --> 00:19:33,268
I'm the eldest daughter, after all.

266
00:19:33,728 --> 00:19:36,138
So I did everything Mom told me to.

267
00:19:36,698 --> 00:19:38,068
I endured the hardships...

268
00:19:38,498 --> 00:19:39,768
gave in even when it was unfair,

269
00:19:40,108 --> 00:19:42,168
and couldn't do a single thing I wanted to.

270
00:19:43,138 --> 00:19:44,338
I gave up on...

271
00:19:46,578 --> 00:19:48,108
the man I loved.

272
00:19:48,278 --> 00:19:49,978
That's how I've lived my life.

273
00:20:12,098 --> 00:20:13,168
Did you spend the night here?

274
00:20:16,178 --> 00:20:18,278
Your house is just a short walk away.

275
00:20:19,208 --> 00:20:23,318
You have so many different ways of making me worry.

276
00:20:26,048 --> 00:20:28,118
But why didn't you answer your phone?

277
00:20:28,518 --> 00:20:29,518
Your phone was ringing,

278
00:20:29,588 --> 00:20:31,158
so it wasn't a problem with your phone.

279
00:20:32,658 --> 00:20:33,858
And your fingers seem fine.

280
00:20:33,928 --> 00:20:35,828
Why didn't you answer? You had me worried.

281
00:20:36,058 --> 00:20:37,458
I'm so frustrated.

282
00:20:39,528 --> 00:20:41,128
Who am I even talking to right now?

283
00:20:42,898 --> 00:20:43,968
Why can't you go home right now?

284
00:20:45,968 --> 00:20:47,608
We have a guest.

285
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:49,538
What?

286
00:20:49,738 --> 00:20:50,808
You haven't eaten, have you?

287
00:20:51,638 --> 00:20:53,678
I'll make myself scarce,

288
00:20:53,778 --> 00:20:55,548
so after you get an earful for breakfast,

289
00:20:55,748 --> 00:20:58,318
there's an antacid in the fridge, so make sure to take it.

290
00:21:00,518 --> 00:21:02,588
Is he my son or my friend?

291
00:21:09,628 --> 00:21:10,628
A visitor?

292
00:21:33,418 --> 00:21:34,818
Were you dating a gold digger?

293
00:21:36,658 --> 00:21:39,228
- What? - That's what your mother said.

294
00:21:40,928 --> 00:21:43,698
That the woman you were dating was a gold digger.

295
00:21:50,568 --> 00:21:51,668
She's not like that.

296
00:21:57,778 --> 00:21:59,108
I heard she was a gold digger.

297
00:22:00,748 --> 00:22:02,678
From an incredibly poor family...

298
00:22:03,878 --> 00:22:06,018
with tons of family to support and only a high school diploma.

299
00:22:09,418 --> 00:22:10,858
The fact that she's from a poor family...

300
00:22:10,918 --> 00:22:11,988
with a high school diploma.

301
00:22:12,058 --> 00:22:13,128
Is there something wrong with that?

302
00:22:13,588 --> 00:22:16,898
Out of everyone I know,

303
00:22:17,428 --> 00:22:19,468
she is the wisest, smartest,

304
00:22:19,868 --> 00:22:21,598
most diligent, and wholesome woman there is.

305
00:22:21,768 --> 00:22:24,498
She's a wonderful person, far too good for a guy like me.

306
00:22:25,238 --> 00:22:26,668
Then why did you two break up?

307
00:22:28,908 --> 00:22:31,308
I'm asking why you broke up with such a wonderful person.

308
00:22:32,508 --> 00:22:34,008
Did you break up with her because of what your mom said?

309
00:22:37,118 --> 00:22:38,448
Or did you think about it...

310
00:22:39,618 --> 00:22:41,588
and decide that dating was fine,

311
00:22:42,588 --> 00:22:45,488
but marriage was realistically impossible?

312
00:22:46,858 --> 00:22:48,188
Please, let's stop talking about this.

313
00:22:49,758 --> 00:22:50,958
Neither you, Ma'am, nor I...

314
00:22:51,028 --> 00:22:52,328
No, not anyone...

315
00:22:53,728 --> 00:22:56,138
has the right to speak so carelessly about her.

316
00:22:57,598 --> 00:23:00,208
If you think I'm not good enough for Seo Hyun,

317
00:23:00,308 --> 00:23:02,168
then please direct your criticism only at me.

318
00:23:02,408 --> 00:23:05,008
Why did you date her if you were just going to end it like this?

319
00:23:07,148 --> 00:23:09,348
Why date her if you couldn't take responsibility?

320
00:23:10,618 --> 00:23:13,318
Why did you date her if you couldn't even protect her?

321
00:23:18,888 --> 00:23:20,058
I don't care...

322
00:23:21,688 --> 00:23:24,598
how great and amazing you are,

323
00:23:24,998 --> 00:23:26,228
but when your family...

324
00:23:27,068 --> 00:23:29,768
is so obsessed with status...

325
00:23:29,838 --> 00:23:32,338
and treats others like dirt,

326
00:23:32,908 --> 00:23:34,268
I won't...

327
00:23:35,268 --> 00:23:38,138
give my daughter to you.

328
00:23:40,448 --> 00:23:43,148
So please, just give up now, Mu Jin.

329
00:23:59,158 --> 00:24:00,198
As for me,

330
00:24:01,828 --> 00:24:03,838
maybe it's because I'm a mother to a daughter,

331
00:24:04,338 --> 00:24:06,538
but I can't stop thinking about that other girl.

332
00:24:09,208 --> 00:24:10,838
But she was treated...

333
00:24:12,138 --> 00:24:13,808
like a gold digger by your family.

334
00:24:16,078 --> 00:24:18,348
After enduring all that pain and humiliation,

335
00:24:20,848 --> 00:24:22,918
I can't imagine how she must have felt when she left you.

336
00:24:37,068 --> 00:24:40,508
What? She said she wouldn't allow it over her dead body?

337
00:24:40,568 --> 00:24:42,068
(Chairman Hong OK Seon)

338
00:24:42,138 --> 00:24:44,638
I mean, we take in this hag who came out of nowhere,

339
00:24:44,708 --> 00:24:46,608
treat her like the chairman's wife,

340
00:24:46,778 --> 00:24:48,008
and she still doesn't know her place.

341
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:51,418
She used to be their housekeeper, right?

342
00:24:51,618 --> 00:24:52,818
Exactly.

343
00:24:53,588 --> 00:24:55,018
She seduced the widowed Chairman Jang,

344
00:24:55,088 --> 00:24:56,988
played her cards so slyly,

345
00:24:57,058 --> 00:24:58,688
and even completely bewitched Seo Hyun...

346
00:24:58,758 --> 00:25:01,758
to end up as the lady of the house. So classless.

347
00:25:02,028 --> 00:25:03,328
Seo Hyun is so attached to her.

348
00:25:03,398 --> 00:25:06,028
People who don't know the history think she's Seo Hyun's real mother.

349
00:25:06,598 --> 00:25:10,338
Should I just kidnap that little rat and dump her in the desert?

350
00:25:10,868 --> 00:25:13,308
At least until Mu Jin and Seo Hyun's wedding is over?

351
00:25:15,338 --> 00:25:16,508
But,

352
00:25:16,838 --> 00:25:20,078
why are you so set on becoming in-laws with that woman?

353
00:25:21,048 --> 00:25:24,048
Is it because of that woman? It's because of Chairman Jang.

354
00:25:24,618 --> 00:25:27,788
But how did Chairman Jang's parents...

355
00:25:27,848 --> 00:25:31,188
even allow him to marry their own housekeeper?

356
00:25:31,258 --> 00:25:33,728
Who can change Chairman Jang's mind once it's made up?

357
00:25:34,558 --> 00:25:37,698
Chairman Jang is just like Mu Jin.

358
00:25:38,458 --> 00:25:40,098
Once he sets his sights on something,

359
00:25:40,168 --> 00:25:41,328
he can't see anything else,

360
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:43,098
and he just gets more defiant if you try to stop him.

361
00:25:46,768 --> 00:25:47,808
I'm sorry to interrupt.

362
00:25:47,868 --> 00:25:49,878
He barged in demanding to see you, Ma'am.

363
00:25:49,978 --> 00:25:51,408
What did you say to Gyu Rim?

364
00:25:52,978 --> 00:25:54,448
Secretary Kim, please step out.

365
00:25:56,318 --> 00:25:57,478
Did you...

366
00:25:57,918 --> 00:25:59,278
call her a gold digger?

367
00:26:00,248 --> 00:26:02,518
Why Gyu Rim again? What about Seo Hyun?

368
00:26:02,618 --> 00:26:04,288
Why are you bringing her up again?

369
00:26:04,618 --> 00:26:06,588
I asked if you called Gyu Rim a gold digger.

370
00:26:07,158 --> 00:26:08,158
Who?

371
00:26:08,828 --> 00:26:09,998
Who told you that?

372
00:26:10,628 --> 00:26:11,828
Did Seo Hyun's mother tell you that?

373
00:26:12,758 --> 00:26:14,868
Why is that woman trying to stir up trouble?

374
00:26:14,928 --> 00:26:16,438
What is her endgame?

375
00:26:17,068 --> 00:26:18,738
How is Gyu Rim a gold digger?

376
00:26:19,238 --> 00:26:20,808
Why are you slandering her?

377
00:26:22,008 --> 00:26:23,678
You think there's some special definition of a gold digger?

378
00:26:24,208 --> 00:26:27,408
When a woman seduces a man who is out of her league,

379
00:26:27,478 --> 00:26:28,878
that's what a gold digger is.

380
00:26:28,978 --> 00:26:30,048
Mother.

381
00:26:32,348 --> 00:26:33,418
Yoon Jin.

382
00:26:34,788 --> 00:26:36,458
This kid has completely lost his mind.

383
00:26:36,788 --> 00:26:39,258
He looks like he might get violent.

384
00:26:40,058 --> 00:26:41,658
Why are you bringing up something that's over and done with?

385
00:26:41,888 --> 00:26:43,428
Mom's already at her breaking point...

386
00:26:43,498 --> 00:26:45,558
over this issue with Seo Hyun. All right?

387
00:26:45,698 --> 00:26:47,128
You said you didn't do anything.

388
00:26:48,468 --> 00:26:50,668
You said you did nothing to Gyu Rim.

389
00:26:50,738 --> 00:26:53,738
I didn't do anything. What could we possibly have done?

390
00:26:53,808 --> 00:26:56,208
We didn't lay a single finger on her.

391
00:26:59,478 --> 00:27:01,408
So were you and Mom just playing me this whole time?

392
00:27:01,548 --> 00:27:02,878
What are you talking about?

393
00:27:03,318 --> 00:27:04,418
Han Gyu Rim was the one who recorded herself...

394
00:27:04,478 --> 00:27:06,418
saying she wanted to break up with you and gave it to me...

395
00:27:12,258 --> 00:27:14,158
So Gyu Rim recorded that and gave it to you?

396
00:27:16,158 --> 00:27:18,058
No, that's not what I meant.

397
00:27:18,898 --> 00:27:20,168
So you could play it for me?

398
00:27:21,198 --> 00:27:22,898
So that I would give up on her?

399
00:27:24,498 --> 00:27:25,998
And that's why Gyu Rim left?

400
00:27:26,738 --> 00:27:27,868
No.

401
00:27:28,438 --> 00:27:30,778
- That's not it... - Then what is it?

402
00:27:31,178 --> 00:27:33,608
Did Gyu Rim really take 100,000 dollars from you?

403
00:27:40,148 --> 00:27:41,688
Yoon Jin, get away from him.

404
00:27:41,918 --> 00:27:44,258
If he hits you with those fists, it'll be your funeral today.

405
00:27:44,318 --> 00:27:45,318
Get away, now.

406
00:27:45,988 --> 00:27:48,688
Fine. If you want to hit me, then go ahead. Hit me.

407
00:27:50,658 --> 00:27:53,198
If hitting me will bring you to your senses,

408
00:27:53,198 --> 00:27:54,598
then I'll take it.

409
00:28:00,138 --> 00:28:01,168
And then what?

410
00:28:02,408 --> 00:28:05,508
Are you going to dump Seo Hyun and go back to Gyu Rim?

411
00:28:08,108 --> 00:28:09,948
You're the one who convinced Seo Hyun to stay...

412
00:28:10,018 --> 00:28:11,318
when she wanted to leave, right?

413
00:28:12,078 --> 00:28:14,518
You've already made one woman cry tears of blood.

414
00:28:14,588 --> 00:28:15,748
Don't do it a second time.

415
00:28:16,718 --> 00:28:18,618
Don't you know what they say about a woman scorned?

416
00:28:18,788 --> 00:28:20,758
"Hell hath no fury like a woman scorned."

417
00:28:55,588 --> 00:28:56,598
Should I heat it up for you?

418
00:29:00,068 --> 00:29:03,098
I love that you're not a picky eater and will eat anything.

419
00:29:09,038 --> 00:29:12,238
And I even made you hangover soup.

420
00:29:12,478 --> 00:29:13,708
You must be so touched, right?

421
00:29:14,178 --> 00:29:15,178
If you are, that'll be 50 cents.

422
00:29:18,418 --> 00:29:19,718
Seven years ago,

423
00:29:21,588 --> 00:29:23,458
I got Mom's number from her friend...

424
00:29:24,688 --> 00:29:26,728
and called her once.

425
00:29:30,398 --> 00:29:31,628
Why would you call her?

426
00:29:32,928 --> 00:29:34,368
She remarried a rich man...

427
00:29:34,768 --> 00:29:37,068
and cut off all contact with you guys and me.

428
00:29:38,268 --> 00:29:40,508
That heartless woman is living just fine.

429
00:29:42,668 --> 00:29:45,008
I told her I was having a really, really hard time.

430
00:29:49,848 --> 00:29:51,048
I asked her to come see me just once.

431
00:29:54,818 --> 00:29:56,888
I said I missed her so much,

432
00:29:58,418 --> 00:29:59,518
but...

433
00:30:01,658 --> 00:30:03,398
she said her daughter was having her appendix out.

434
00:30:05,698 --> 00:30:06,928
She said she was sorry,

435
00:30:07,768 --> 00:30:09,628
but she couldn't come.

436
00:30:10,738 --> 00:30:11,738
What?

437
00:30:17,608 --> 00:30:19,638
After that, I blocked her number.

438
00:30:21,778 --> 00:30:22,778
Good for you.

439
00:30:23,678 --> 00:30:24,748
That cruel woman.

440
00:30:26,718 --> 00:30:30,158
She's always been sharp as a knife and a bit cold, you know.

441
00:30:33,288 --> 00:30:35,228
Why aren't you eating more?

442
00:30:37,358 --> 00:30:38,898
I can't stand to look at you either, Dad.

443
00:30:39,528 --> 00:30:40,628
What?

444
00:30:43,838 --> 00:30:44,998
I think I'm going to throw up.

445
00:30:45,768 --> 00:30:47,168
What?

446
00:30:48,008 --> 00:30:49,338
Hey!

447
00:30:50,778 --> 00:30:51,778
I mean...

448
00:30:52,278 --> 00:30:53,678
What in the world is going on?

449
00:30:54,208 --> 00:30:56,748
Hey, if you leave like that, I'll be really hurt.

450
00:30:58,548 --> 00:31:00,888
I'll never understand women.

451
00:31:33,288 --> 00:31:34,918
(Jung Woo)

452
00:31:36,958 --> 00:31:39,088
- Hello. - Where are you?

453
00:31:40,028 --> 00:31:41,288
I said, where are you?

454
00:31:45,828 --> 00:31:46,828
In front of Gyu Rim's house.

455
00:31:47,428 --> 00:31:50,298
Are you crazy? What are you doing there?

456
00:31:51,568 --> 00:31:52,568
That's what I'm saying.

457
00:31:53,098 --> 00:31:54,108
Why did I come here?

458
00:31:54,538 --> 00:31:58,578
Are you some kind of hero? Anyway, start your car right now,

459
00:31:58,638 --> 00:32:00,208
set your GPS for the restaurant, and get here now.

460
00:32:00,748 --> 00:32:02,208
If you can't drive, I'll come get you.

461
00:32:02,878 --> 00:32:05,248
No. I can drive.

462
00:32:05,378 --> 00:32:06,378
I'm heading there now.

463
00:32:25,268 --> 00:32:26,838
Yes, I'm okay, ma'am.

464
00:32:26,908 --> 00:32:28,138
I'm just leaving the house now.

465
00:32:28,538 --> 00:32:29,878
Okay, see you soon.

466
00:33:01,008 --> 00:33:03,838
I have my ID. I have my cards.

467
00:33:05,508 --> 00:33:07,578
And I have all my cash.

468
00:33:32,238 --> 00:33:33,238
Are you okay?

469
00:33:35,268 --> 00:33:37,108
- Did you lose something? - Yes.

470
00:33:37,478 --> 00:33:38,478
What is it?

471
00:33:45,248 --> 00:33:46,888
Dad, can you lift your foot?

472
00:33:48,348 --> 00:33:49,518
Don't talk to me.

473
00:33:49,718 --> 00:33:51,218
I'm really hurt.

474
00:33:52,518 --> 00:33:55,128
Of all people, how could you say something like that to me?

475
00:34:10,808 --> 00:34:12,538
Hey.

476
00:34:15,248 --> 00:34:16,248
What are you doing?

477
00:34:17,148 --> 00:34:19,018
There's nothing under his foot.

478
00:34:19,618 --> 00:34:23,618
Hey. I said I'm really hurt. Don't talk to me.

479
00:34:23,688 --> 00:34:26,888
I didn't talk to you. I just lifted your foot.

480
00:34:29,128 --> 00:34:30,128
You hit really hard.

481
00:34:43,208 --> 00:34:45,478
So what is it? What did you lose?

482
00:34:46,878 --> 00:34:49,178
Money? Your ID?

483
00:34:50,078 --> 00:34:52,448
- Your cards? - No, I have all of those.

484
00:34:53,348 --> 00:34:55,088
Then what is it? I can't help you look...

485
00:34:55,148 --> 00:34:56,388
if I don't know what it is.

486
00:34:57,458 --> 00:34:58,458
That's just it.

487
00:34:59,988 --> 00:35:01,358
I don't know what it is.

488
00:35:02,358 --> 00:35:04,528
I'm sure I lost something.

489
00:35:06,128 --> 00:35:08,328
But I don't know what I lost.

490
00:35:10,798 --> 00:35:12,198
Are you still drunk?

491
00:35:12,738 --> 00:35:13,738
Should I get you some medicine?

492
00:35:17,938 --> 00:35:20,248
(Kkokkobyeol Cart Bar)

493
00:35:47,338 --> 00:35:48,508
All right, let's see.

494
00:35:48,608 --> 00:35:49,608
(Suragan Side Dishes)

495
00:35:53,908 --> 00:35:54,948
What's this?

496
00:35:55,508 --> 00:35:58,548
Oh, you're here? What do you think it is?

497
00:35:58,818 --> 00:36:02,618
This is to celebrate Han Gyu Rim and Jo Heung Sik's new beginning.

498
00:36:02,688 --> 00:36:05,488
It's a special event from me. Buy one, get one free.

499
00:36:09,058 --> 00:36:10,798
But how are you feeling?

500
00:36:11,398 --> 00:36:12,458
When you have indigestion,

501
00:36:12,528 --> 00:36:14,198
you're supposed to rest no matter what.

502
00:36:15,368 --> 00:36:17,568
Heung Sik hasn't even agreed to it yet.

503
00:36:18,668 --> 00:36:20,138
If he takes me back,

504
00:36:20,238 --> 00:36:22,108
let's do the event once things are certain.

505
00:36:22,168 --> 00:36:23,168
Goodness.

506
00:36:23,608 --> 00:36:27,108
We don't need to ask him for his opinion.

507
00:36:27,478 --> 00:36:28,808
If I say it's okay,

508
00:36:28,878 --> 00:36:31,678
he's automatically okay with it too, you hear?

509
00:36:32,618 --> 00:36:35,988
- But still... - My goodness, you're persistent.

510
00:36:36,318 --> 00:36:39,288
All right.

511
00:36:40,328 --> 00:36:42,688
I'll go right now...

512
00:36:42,828 --> 00:36:45,358
and feed him his favourite pork bone soup.

513
00:36:45,758 --> 00:36:47,198
And I'll get his agreement. That should work, right?

514
00:36:48,728 --> 00:36:50,298
Oh dear, what am I going to do?

515
00:36:51,938 --> 00:36:53,298
At two thirty,

516
00:36:53,738 --> 00:36:55,568
Mr. Oh from Majang-dong is supposed to come by,

517
00:36:56,168 --> 00:37:00,178
- and I completely forgot about it. - Then I'll go see Heung Sik.

518
00:37:00,248 --> 00:37:04,918
Oh, would you? Great, then that's a big help to me.

519
00:37:05,618 --> 00:37:07,688
Heung Sik will be over the moon, won't he?

520
00:37:09,548 --> 00:37:11,658
- I'll get going. - Okay, you do that.

521
00:37:12,188 --> 00:37:14,258
- Go on, hurry back. - Okay.

522
00:37:16,088 --> 00:37:17,828
This worked out perfectly.

523
00:37:27,838 --> 00:37:29,868
Heung Sik, the food's ready.

524
00:37:30,478 --> 00:37:31,478
Let's eat.

525
00:37:32,678 --> 00:37:33,678
Here.

526
00:37:36,108 --> 00:37:37,118
Heung Sik.

527
00:37:38,218 --> 00:37:40,118
The pork bone soup turned out really delicious, Heung Sik.

528
00:37:41,448 --> 00:37:42,618
Stop.

529
00:37:43,048 --> 00:37:45,058
Hey, how close are you trying to get?

530
00:37:46,288 --> 00:37:47,388
Aren't you going to eat?

531
00:37:49,088 --> 00:37:50,628
I'm not going to let you feed me.

532
00:37:51,628 --> 00:37:52,628
Why?

533
00:37:54,168 --> 00:37:56,468
Well, when you're close to me,

534
00:37:57,238 --> 00:37:59,068
I can't breathe properly,

535
00:37:59,668 --> 00:38:03,038
and my heart beats too fast. Anyway, just don't come near me.

536
00:38:04,608 --> 00:38:06,378
You have an arrhythmia, remember?

537
00:38:08,048 --> 00:38:09,208
That's all the more reason.

538
00:38:09,848 --> 00:38:11,748
Just leave it there. I'll eat on my own.

539
00:38:11,918 --> 00:38:13,448
How are you going to eat on your own?

540
00:38:13,518 --> 00:38:14,788
You can't use your arm.

541
00:38:15,618 --> 00:38:18,188
I can just ask Gyu Oh to come over.

542
00:38:18,558 --> 00:38:19,758
Gyu Oh has work to do today.

543
00:38:21,658 --> 00:38:22,788
I can ask my mom to come.

544
00:38:23,628 --> 00:38:25,458
Your mom has plans today.

545
00:38:31,068 --> 00:38:32,068
Is it happening now?

546
00:38:32,738 --> 00:38:34,038
Is it hard for you to breathe?

547
00:38:35,168 --> 00:38:36,408
Should I check your pulse?

548
00:38:39,678 --> 00:38:41,208
Hey, wait, just a second.

549
00:38:44,378 --> 00:38:47,518
Okay, I'm going. I'm leaving, so just relax.

550
00:38:51,518 --> 00:38:52,518
To you,

551
00:38:53,518 --> 00:38:54,888
I must seem crazy, right?

552
00:38:57,858 --> 00:38:59,658
I'm not exactly normal either.

553
00:39:02,128 --> 00:39:04,398
I lost something yesterday,

554
00:39:05,998 --> 00:39:07,408
but I don't know what it was.

555
00:39:09,608 --> 00:39:11,378
No matter how hard I think,

556
00:39:12,208 --> 00:39:13,378
I can't remember what it is.

557
00:39:15,148 --> 00:39:16,148
Really?

558
00:39:46,878 --> 00:39:48,208
(Father)

559
00:39:49,308 --> 00:39:50,318
Darn it.

560
00:39:50,878 --> 00:39:51,878
Darn...

561
00:39:57,888 --> 00:40:00,528
I heard you got into a fight with a patient and were fired.

562
00:40:02,688 --> 00:40:03,698
Darn it.

563
00:40:05,828 --> 00:40:08,198
How did you find out? Who told you?

564
00:40:10,028 --> 00:40:12,798
I went to the hospital you used to work for and a nurse told me. Why?

565
00:40:13,468 --> 00:40:15,508
Dad, why would you go there?

566
00:40:15,808 --> 00:40:17,408
I went for a skincare treatment.

567
00:40:17,608 --> 00:40:19,378
Your wedding's just around the corner.

568
00:40:20,008 --> 00:40:22,048
I guess a leopard doesn't change its spots.

569
00:40:22,408 --> 00:40:23,548
You're even fighting with patients now?

570
00:40:24,348 --> 00:40:26,648
Why do you care if I get into fights?

571
00:40:27,018 --> 00:40:29,548
You've become a real brawler. This isn't good.

572
00:40:30,048 --> 00:40:31,188
At this rate, you'll pick a fight with me...

573
00:40:31,258 --> 00:40:32,258
while I'm walking you down the aisle.

574
00:40:32,418 --> 00:40:33,758
Your big comeback is cancelled.

575
00:40:33,988 --> 00:40:35,158
You don't have to come to the wedding.

576
00:40:35,788 --> 00:40:36,788
What?

577
00:40:36,858 --> 00:40:39,528
I'll just go back to pretending you're dead.

578
00:40:39,658 --> 00:40:41,468
Hey, you can't do that.

579
00:40:41,698 --> 00:40:43,868
You broke your promise too.

580
00:40:43,998 --> 00:40:45,538
I asked you to break up Jo Heung Sik and Han Gyu Rim,

581
00:40:45,638 --> 00:40:47,308
but I hear they've decided to officially start dating.

582
00:40:47,438 --> 00:40:48,668
So, you'll take your perfectly healthy father...

583
00:40:48,738 --> 00:40:50,208
and kill him, revive him, then kill him again?

584
00:40:50,438 --> 00:40:51,438
What am I, a piece of frozen fish?

585
00:40:51,638 --> 00:40:53,008
That you can just thaw out and freeze again?

586
00:40:54,178 --> 00:40:55,278
Well then,

587
00:40:55,578 --> 00:40:57,818
you should have lived a more respectable life.

588
00:40:57,918 --> 00:40:59,248
You didn't have to be a father I could be proud of,

589
00:40:59,318 --> 00:41:01,548
but you shouldn't have been one I was ashamed of.

590
00:41:01,618 --> 00:41:02,748
Hey, did you two plan this?

591
00:41:03,758 --> 00:41:04,918
Did you and Gyu Rim plan this together?

592
00:41:05,118 --> 00:41:06,118
Hey.

593
00:41:06,688 --> 00:41:09,358
Hey, you think I wanted to live my life this way?

594
00:41:09,658 --> 00:41:11,358
This is so upsetting, really.

595
00:41:12,828 --> 00:41:14,698
What did I do that was so wrong?

596
00:41:14,898 --> 00:41:16,098
(Chairman Jang)

597
00:41:18,968 --> 00:41:21,538
Don't tell the family I quit my job.

598
00:41:21,738 --> 00:41:23,568
And especially don't tell Han Gyu Rim.

599
00:41:23,638 --> 00:41:24,638
Do you under...

600
00:41:28,478 --> 00:41:30,248
Darn it.

601
00:41:34,748 --> 00:41:35,748
Yes, Chairman.

602
00:41:36,918 --> 00:41:39,688
(Danim-Gil Knife-Cut Noodles)

603
00:41:54,568 --> 00:41:55,608
What are you doing?

604
00:41:59,508 --> 00:42:00,508
Oh, ma'am.

605
00:42:00,748 --> 00:42:02,948
What are you doing? Trying to end it all in a bowl of soup?

606
00:42:04,318 --> 00:42:05,378
How did you know?

607
00:42:05,518 --> 00:42:06,518
Good grief.

608
00:42:09,588 --> 00:42:10,588
Oh, for heaven's sake.

609
00:42:10,658 --> 00:42:12,058
(Danim-Gil Knife-Cut Noodles)

610
00:42:12,118 --> 00:42:14,258
You've got a knack for comedy.

611
00:42:14,558 --> 00:42:16,088
Do I look like I'm joking?

612
00:42:16,228 --> 00:42:19,128
So you're actually, sincerely trying to kill yourself?

613
00:42:20,128 --> 00:42:23,128
If you hadn't shown up, I could have actually died.

614
00:42:25,138 --> 00:42:26,498
Did something happen?

615
00:42:28,938 --> 00:42:31,308
Something that would make a man want to drown himself in a saucer.

616
00:42:33,848 --> 00:42:34,848
Problems with your wife?

617
00:42:37,248 --> 00:42:38,448
I don't have a wife.

618
00:42:39,018 --> 00:42:40,018
Problems with your children?

619
00:42:45,018 --> 00:42:48,258
Well, pour me a glass too. Ma'am, one soju glass over here...

620
00:42:48,728 --> 00:42:50,258
Actually, just bring us a bottle of soju.

621
00:42:50,498 --> 00:42:52,158
I don't think one glass will cut it for me today.

622
00:42:52,258 --> 00:42:53,658
I'm just going to drink straight from the bottle.

623
00:42:54,298 --> 00:42:56,068
No, you should just drink by the glass.

624
00:42:56,128 --> 00:42:57,128
It's bad for your health.

625
00:42:57,398 --> 00:42:58,398
Look at me.

626
00:43:00,438 --> 00:43:01,808
I'm drinking by the glass...

627
00:43:02,038 --> 00:43:03,368
for my health too.

628
00:43:04,508 --> 00:43:05,508
No.

629
00:43:10,818 --> 00:43:13,078
Want to bet on whose kid is a bigger disappointment?

630
00:43:14,918 --> 00:43:17,988
- Let's do it. You're on. - You go first.

631
00:43:19,758 --> 00:43:20,758
My oldest daughter.

632
00:43:21,728 --> 00:43:23,588
I even made her hangover soup,

633
00:43:24,558 --> 00:43:25,828
and she says she can't stand the sight of me.

634
00:43:26,728 --> 00:43:27,728
That I make her sick.

635
00:43:30,328 --> 00:43:31,998
I have only one son.

636
00:43:33,698 --> 00:43:36,538
My husband died young, so I raised him like a prince,

637
00:43:38,738 --> 00:43:41,248
but he left me for some woman.

638
00:43:42,578 --> 00:43:44,178
He showed up today for the first time in years...

639
00:43:44,248 --> 00:43:47,748
only to take that girl's side. I was just so furious.

640
00:43:53,988 --> 00:43:55,328
My second daughter.

641
00:43:56,258 --> 00:43:59,128
She didn't want me at her wedding,

642
00:44:00,228 --> 00:44:01,528
so she told her in-laws...

643
00:44:02,468 --> 00:44:03,468
I was dead.

644
00:44:04,038 --> 00:44:05,798
What? For real?

645
00:44:06,768 --> 00:44:07,808
That rotten girl.

646
00:44:09,508 --> 00:44:10,708
Are you insulting my daughter?

647
00:44:11,508 --> 00:44:12,508
Okay, you win.

648
00:44:12,678 --> 00:44:14,708
You really do have a reason to want to die of shame.

649
00:44:15,678 --> 00:44:16,678
That rotten punk.

650
00:44:18,218 --> 00:44:19,818
Are you insulting my son?

651
00:44:21,048 --> 00:44:22,648
You started it.

652
00:44:22,818 --> 00:44:25,618
You should want to die of shame right along with me.

653
00:44:26,758 --> 00:44:28,488
Hey, why are you suddenly speaking so informally?

654
00:44:28,788 --> 00:44:30,028
When someone younger gets cheeky,

655
00:44:30,088 --> 00:44:32,328
I drop the formalities without thinking. Why?

656
00:44:33,028 --> 00:44:34,098
How old are you?

657
00:44:34,428 --> 00:44:36,368
You look at least five years younger than me. What did you say?

658
00:44:36,468 --> 00:44:37,468
Look who's talking.

659
00:44:37,568 --> 00:44:39,468
You look ten years younger than me. How dare you?

660
00:44:39,898 --> 00:44:41,008
Let's see your ID.

661
00:44:41,268 --> 00:44:44,008
You think I'm afraid to show you mine?

662
00:44:44,078 --> 00:44:46,538
(Hong OK Seon, born in 1967, Han Seok Joong, born in 1969)

663
00:44:46,608 --> 00:44:48,548
See? I'm two years older than you.

664
00:44:51,848 --> 00:44:52,878
No way.

665
00:44:53,478 --> 00:44:54,788
How can this face...

666
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:57,718
You could pass for someone in their 40s.

667
00:44:57,958 --> 00:45:00,288
Isn't this some kind of scam?

668
00:45:01,328 --> 00:45:04,128
Seriously, how can you look so young for your age?

669
00:45:05,428 --> 00:45:06,558
Is it a crime to look young?

670
00:45:08,028 --> 00:45:10,968
If you mess with me again, you're dead.

671
00:45:12,068 --> 00:45:13,898
- Yes, ma'am. - Understood?

672
00:45:14,308 --> 00:45:15,308
Yes.

673
00:45:16,668 --> 00:45:17,678
You're very busy, aren't you?

674
00:45:19,108 --> 00:45:20,108
It's all right.

675
00:45:20,808 --> 00:45:23,648
After you left my office the other day,

676
00:45:25,278 --> 00:45:26,918
it kept bothering me.

677
00:45:28,448 --> 00:45:31,588
I felt like maybe I was only talking from my own point of view.

678
00:45:34,658 --> 00:45:37,028
It's not like you're going to come to my wedding, though.

679
00:45:42,298 --> 00:45:43,298
Take this.

680
00:45:45,098 --> 00:45:47,238
- What is this? - A wedding gift.

681
00:45:49,308 --> 00:45:51,108
Are you trying to buy your way out of guilt?

682
00:45:53,138 --> 00:45:55,978
Well, maybe. Open it and see if I can.

683
00:46:00,918 --> 00:46:02,918
(Cashier's Check: 100,000 dollars)

684
00:46:07,158 --> 00:46:08,228
Does my mother know?

685
00:46:09,358 --> 00:46:10,388
No.

686
00:46:11,228 --> 00:46:12,758
And this has nothing to do with your mother.

687
00:46:13,558 --> 00:46:15,128
I'm giving this to you because I want to.

688
00:46:19,468 --> 00:46:21,438
You must be really rich.

689
00:46:22,608 --> 00:46:24,778
Giving 100,000 dollars as a wedding gift.

690
00:46:26,108 --> 00:46:27,108
Gyu Young.

691
00:46:27,878 --> 00:46:29,878
I told you this before, didn't I?

692
00:46:31,248 --> 00:46:34,288
If you're a daughter to my wife, you're like a child to me too.

693
00:46:35,688 --> 00:46:36,688
That's right.

694
00:46:37,618 --> 00:46:39,158
You know, later on,

695
00:46:40,118 --> 00:46:42,858
when you've softened up a bit toward your mother,

696
00:46:44,198 --> 00:46:46,128
I'd like it if you came to visit us at home.

697
00:46:46,458 --> 00:46:49,268
Then I could introduce you to our Seo Hyun...

698
00:46:49,928 --> 00:46:50,968
Right.

699
00:46:51,468 --> 00:46:53,968
I'd also like to meet your older sister and younger brother.

700
00:46:57,038 --> 00:46:58,778
Later, when you're ready.

701
00:47:01,648 --> 00:47:02,648
This is so annoying.

702
00:47:05,648 --> 00:47:08,688
I envy your daughter so much.

703
00:47:10,148 --> 00:47:11,958
it makes me so jealous and annoyed.

704
00:47:13,288 --> 00:47:16,958
Why aren't you my dad? Why is my dad so pathetic...

705
00:47:17,028 --> 00:47:18,728
and why are you so cool?

706
00:47:20,098 --> 00:47:21,468
It really upsets me.

707
00:47:22,968 --> 00:47:24,768
This is so annoying.

708
00:47:31,238 --> 00:47:32,238
Don't follow me.

709
00:47:33,078 --> 00:47:34,078
Because of you,

710
00:47:37,108 --> 00:47:38,948
I miss Kim Mu Jin like crazy now.

711
00:48:04,208 --> 00:48:05,208
Mu Jin.

712
00:48:07,708 --> 00:48:08,778
Are you feeling okay?

713
00:48:09,578 --> 00:48:13,278
Yes, I'm all better. I'm perfectly back to normal.

714
00:48:14,418 --> 00:48:15,418
Good.

715
00:48:16,048 --> 00:48:17,048
That's great.

716
00:48:19,388 --> 00:48:20,388
Hey.

717
00:48:20,988 --> 00:48:23,088
I can't come see you for a while.

718
00:48:23,588 --> 00:48:26,958
My mom said if I see you, she'll disown me.

719
00:48:27,158 --> 00:48:28,598
She holds such a grudge.

720
00:48:30,028 --> 00:48:31,038
I'm sorry.

721
00:48:31,768 --> 00:48:35,108
My mom is really strange, but just give me a little more time.

722
00:48:35,668 --> 00:48:38,278
I've waited 23 years for you, since I was ten.

723
00:48:38,478 --> 00:48:40,478
So please, just wait for me a little longer.

724
00:48:41,808 --> 00:48:43,348
It won't take another 23 years, though.

725
00:48:45,018 --> 00:48:47,318
- Seo Hyun. - I'm listening.

726
00:48:51,358 --> 00:48:53,518
What? What are you trying to say?

727
00:48:57,828 --> 00:49:01,268
What is this? I have a bad feeling. I don't want to hear it.

728
00:49:01,728 --> 00:49:03,628
Let's hang up, Mu Jin. I have to go to the bathroom.

729
00:49:04,238 --> 00:49:06,238
- Seo Hyun... - Bye, Mu Jin. I love you.

730
00:49:06,698 --> 00:49:08,368
I love you more than anyone on Earth.

731
00:49:08,708 --> 00:49:09,708
Bye.

732
00:49:20,918 --> 00:49:23,548
You have a visitor.

733
00:49:24,558 --> 00:49:25,558
Who?

734
00:49:26,658 --> 00:49:27,658
Han Gyeol.

735
00:49:31,358 --> 00:49:33,498
Tell him I'm not here. That I didn't come to work today.

736
00:49:34,398 --> 00:49:36,068
I was going to.

737
00:49:36,698 --> 00:49:39,868
Why am I like this? Why can't I lie to a child?

738
00:49:42,868 --> 00:49:45,108
Just tell him you thought I was here, but I'm not.

739
00:49:46,708 --> 00:49:49,848
Okay. Got it. For Han Gyeol's sake, too,

740
00:49:50,578 --> 00:49:52,648
it's better to draw the line right here.

741
00:49:53,078 --> 00:49:56,288
I'll do my best to lie to him.

742
00:50:12,498 --> 00:50:13,498
Han Gyeol.

743
00:50:15,568 --> 00:50:16,738
Mister.

744
00:50:31,388 --> 00:50:32,388
Is it good?

745
00:50:32,458 --> 00:50:33,458
Yes.

746
00:50:41,698 --> 00:50:42,768
That's a relief.

747
00:50:44,268 --> 00:50:45,268
What is?

748
00:50:45,438 --> 00:50:47,498
I came here to see you one last time.

749
00:50:48,168 --> 00:50:49,668
So I'm glad we could meet like this.

750
00:50:51,408 --> 00:50:52,408
Last time?

751
00:50:53,138 --> 00:50:56,178
I don't think I should come see you anymore.

752
00:50:58,618 --> 00:50:59,818
Your mom...

753
00:51:07,188 --> 00:51:08,428
I was thinking the same thing.

754
00:51:09,388 --> 00:51:10,788
We think alike, even at the very end.

755
00:51:11,228 --> 00:51:12,228
I knew it.

756
00:51:15,298 --> 00:51:16,668
For one last time,

757
00:51:17,498 --> 00:51:18,968
should we shake hands before we go?

758
00:51:19,998 --> 00:51:21,408
Before we do,

759
00:51:22,808 --> 00:51:24,508
there's one last thing I want to say.

760
00:51:27,138 --> 00:51:28,148
What is it?

761
00:51:28,208 --> 00:51:31,318
I don't want to lie to you.

762
00:51:34,248 --> 00:51:38,758
My mom and Jo Heung Sik aren't married yet.

763
00:51:41,628 --> 00:51:42,628
I know.

764
00:51:43,558 --> 00:51:44,658
I found out a little while ago.

765
00:51:45,258 --> 00:51:46,358
You knew?

766
00:51:46,758 --> 00:51:48,728
Then why did you pretend you didn't know?

767
00:51:53,498 --> 00:51:56,438
I wanted to respect your mom's decision.

768
00:51:57,938 --> 00:51:59,208
Even her lying...

769
00:51:59,908 --> 00:52:01,378
was her decision to make.

770
00:52:02,908 --> 00:52:03,978
But...

771
00:52:04,878 --> 00:52:07,718
she did propose to Jo Heung Sik.

772
00:52:10,388 --> 00:52:11,388
Is that so?

773
00:52:13,258 --> 00:52:14,258
I see.

774
00:52:17,388 --> 00:52:19,728
Then let's shake hands now, for the last time.

775
00:52:24,268 --> 00:52:25,498
Take care, Han Gyeol.

776
00:52:26,038 --> 00:52:27,098
Stay healthy.

777
00:52:27,438 --> 00:52:29,568
You stay healthy and take care too.

778
00:53:07,978 --> 00:53:09,348
Who? Han Gyu Oh?

779
00:53:10,078 --> 00:53:12,648
Yes, he's a friend of my boyfriend's friend.

780
00:53:13,248 --> 00:53:14,348
You don't know him?

781
00:53:15,088 --> 00:53:16,348
From the way he looked at your picture,

782
00:53:16,418 --> 00:53:17,788
I thought you two had a dramatic history.

783
00:53:20,918 --> 00:53:22,158
He's not a stalker, is he?

784
00:53:22,728 --> 00:53:24,128
Did I make a mistake bringing it up?

785
00:53:25,958 --> 00:53:26,958
So?

786
00:53:27,898 --> 00:53:29,828
I just showed him your picture.

787
00:53:30,268 --> 00:53:32,668
I didn't give him your number or your social media or anything.

788
00:53:33,898 --> 00:53:34,908
But...

789
00:53:35,038 --> 00:53:36,708
he was really handsome.

790
00:53:37,008 --> 00:53:38,108
He's totally my type.

791
00:53:38,678 --> 00:53:41,008
If he wasn't into you, I might've tried to steal him.

792
00:53:43,008 --> 00:53:45,018
Oh, I almost forgot.

793
00:53:45,678 --> 00:53:47,318
Han Gyu Oh asked me to pass on a message.

794
00:53:47,448 --> 00:53:48,618
Tonight at 8p.m.,

795
00:53:48,688 --> 00:53:50,418
he's going to be waiting at Haeona Park,

796
00:53:50,788 --> 00:53:52,588
and he wants you to come if you're interested in meeting him.

797
00:53:52,888 --> 00:53:54,018
He said he'll be waiting.

798
00:53:54,528 --> 00:53:56,858
Anyway, I texted you Han Gyu Oh's number.

799
00:54:06,498 --> 00:54:08,068
Let me know if you're not going.

800
00:54:09,568 --> 00:54:11,208
Because if you don't want to go, I will.

801
00:54:49,448 --> 00:54:50,648
I look just like a gigolo.

802
00:55:26,618 --> 00:55:27,918
All done.

803
00:55:28,488 --> 00:55:29,588
Okay.

804
00:55:40,028 --> 00:55:41,398
(Han Gyu Oh)

805
00:55:41,468 --> 00:55:42,968
(Copy Text)

806
00:55:43,028 --> 00:55:44,228
(Copied)

807
00:55:45,668 --> 00:55:47,438
(Paste)

808
00:55:47,498 --> 00:55:51,068
(Gigolo Bastard)

809
00:55:51,138 --> 00:55:52,308
Why is this jerk's number coming up?

810
00:55:56,108 --> 00:55:57,648
(Han Gyu Oh)

811
00:55:57,708 --> 00:55:59,018
(Copy Text)

812
00:56:00,118 --> 00:56:01,918
(Paste)

813
00:56:01,988 --> 00:56:04,988
(Gigolo Bastard)

814
00:56:06,788 --> 00:56:10,188
Why are Han Gyu Oh's number and that Gigolo's number the same?

815
00:56:11,798 --> 00:56:12,898
Han Gyu Oh...

816
00:56:14,928 --> 00:56:16,228
was the gigolo?

817
00:57:29,208 --> 00:57:32,208
Excuse me, were there any lost items yesterday?

818
00:57:32,808 --> 00:57:34,978
The phone was picked up earlier,

819
00:57:35,578 --> 00:57:37,108
and the hat was picked up a little while ago.

820
00:57:37,778 --> 00:57:38,918
What did you lose?

821
00:57:39,978 --> 00:57:42,548
I'm not exactly sure what it is.

822
00:57:43,988 --> 00:57:44,988
Excuse me?

823
00:57:45,418 --> 00:57:46,458
I know it sounds absurd.

824
00:57:46,658 --> 00:57:48,258
I know it must sound completely absurd,

825
00:57:48,928 --> 00:57:50,928
but I'm sure I lost something.

826
00:57:52,798 --> 00:57:56,368
So you're saying you lost something,

827
00:57:57,198 --> 00:58:00,598
but you don't know what you lost?

828
00:58:01,938 --> 00:58:02,938
Yes.

829
00:58:03,408 --> 00:58:04,908
Well, then...

830
00:58:05,378 --> 00:58:07,078
Leave your phone number or a business card.

831
00:58:07,138 --> 00:58:09,378
If anything turns up, I'll text or call you.

832
00:58:10,408 --> 00:58:11,718
Okay, thank you.

833
00:58:23,028 --> 00:58:25,628
I came out this way...

834
00:58:29,628 --> 00:58:31,468
and I must have walked over here.

835
00:58:38,178 --> 00:58:39,178
Gyu Rim.

836
00:58:40,138 --> 00:58:41,208
What has gotten into you?

837
00:58:41,878 --> 00:58:44,048
Someone helped me.

838
00:58:44,348 --> 00:58:45,418
Get up.

839
00:58:45,618 --> 00:58:48,388
Thank you. You can go now.

840
00:59:05,538 --> 00:59:07,198
Thank you.

841
00:59:15,648 --> 00:59:16,708
Who was that?

842
00:59:31,458 --> 00:59:33,158
Who in the world are you?

843
01:00:04,728 --> 01:00:06,398
Chef, did you burn your hand?

844
01:00:06,998 --> 01:00:08,228
I'll go get the first-aid kit.

845
01:00:13,738 --> 01:00:15,038
Just this once.

846
01:00:15,938 --> 01:00:17,408
I saw you helping with closing.

847
01:00:18,208 --> 01:00:20,108
You're a quick learner, and you seem genuinely sorry.

848
01:00:20,738 --> 01:00:22,408
And I can tell you're eager to make things right,

849
01:00:22,408 --> 01:00:24,108
so I'm giving you just one pass.

850
01:00:24,308 --> 01:00:28,618
Thank you. I promise I will never be even a second late again.

851
01:00:37,028 --> 01:00:38,028
Gyu Min?

852
01:00:39,398 --> 01:00:40,798
It's you, right?

853
01:00:42,428 --> 01:00:43,998
What's going on with you two?

854
01:00:46,138 --> 01:00:50,308
No, wait, why and how do you two know each other?

855
01:00:51,908 --> 01:00:54,438
No, it can't be.

856
01:00:56,178 --> 01:00:57,178
It is.

857
01:00:57,948 --> 01:00:59,148
She's Gyu Rim's sister.

858
01:01:02,218 --> 01:01:04,418
This is your restaurant?

859
01:01:05,288 --> 01:01:06,488
Yes.

860
01:01:07,418 --> 01:01:09,188
So you're the new hire we brought on.

861
01:01:10,028 --> 01:01:11,028
Yes.

862
01:01:11,558 --> 01:01:13,628
I'll do my best.

863
01:01:15,328 --> 01:01:17,528
Great. I look forward to working with you too.

864
01:01:19,638 --> 01:01:23,368
Gyu Oh said that Gyu Rim lost something and couldn't find it.

865
01:01:23,538 --> 01:01:26,038
That's why I was late. I was helping her look for it.

866
01:01:26,108 --> 01:01:27,108
What was it?

867
01:01:27,478 --> 01:01:30,248
- What did she lose? - That's what I'm talking about.

868
01:01:30,408 --> 01:01:33,048
That's the crazy part. She doesn't know.

869
01:01:33,178 --> 01:01:34,518
It's hard enough to find something even when you know what you've lost.

870
01:01:34,578 --> 01:01:36,488
How are you supposed to find it if you don't even know what it is?

871
01:01:37,448 --> 01:01:38,818
Do you think maybe Gyu Rim hit her head...

872
01:01:38,888 --> 01:01:39,888
on her way home drunk?

873
01:01:41,688 --> 01:01:44,388
Right? That's what I was thinking too.

874
01:01:45,128 --> 01:01:47,398
What if Gyu Rim got mugged or something,

875
01:01:47,458 --> 01:01:49,228
got hit in the head, and now something's wrong?

876
01:01:49,368 --> 01:01:50,628
What would we do then?

877
01:01:51,128 --> 01:01:53,868
Anyway, I'll see you at home. This is a big deal.

878
01:01:55,168 --> 01:01:58,168
Okay. I'll be home soon.

879
01:02:01,608 --> 01:02:03,178
You scared me.

880
01:02:04,878 --> 01:02:07,448
Is something wrong with your sister?

881
01:02:25,468 --> 01:02:27,238
Did you find what you lost?

882
01:02:31,508 --> 01:02:33,308
I heard you lost something after you got drunk.

883
01:02:34,938 --> 01:02:35,948
Did you find it?

884
01:02:37,108 --> 01:02:38,308
How did you know about that?

885
01:02:43,348 --> 01:02:44,348
No.

886
01:02:46,618 --> 01:02:48,188
Do you have any clues?

887
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:52,598
It's okay.

888
01:02:53,598 --> 01:02:54,998
Don't worry about it.

889
01:02:55,568 --> 01:02:57,068
Did you go back to the bar?

890
01:02:58,768 --> 01:03:01,298
At the convenience store, the crosswalk...

891
01:03:01,668 --> 01:03:02,808
and along the path you took,

892
01:03:02,808 --> 01:03:04,438
I don't remember you dropped anything there.

893
01:03:05,708 --> 01:03:06,808
How did you know about the convenience...

894
01:03:06,808 --> 01:03:07,878
store and the crosswalk?

895
01:03:18,048 --> 01:03:19,658
Gyu Rim. Han Gyu Rim.

896
01:03:20,018 --> 01:03:21,188
Gyu Rim.

897
01:03:31,968 --> 01:03:33,368
What are you doing? You can't just cross like that.

898
01:03:33,438 --> 01:03:34,638
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

899
01:03:36,008 --> 01:03:37,468
It was you, Mu Jin.

900
01:03:45,478 --> 01:03:46,748
Are you feeling okay?

901
01:04:11,738 --> 01:04:13,278
What do I do?

902
01:04:23,248 --> 01:04:24,918
What do I do?

903
01:04:27,188 --> 01:04:28,958
I just remembered.

904
01:04:29,858 --> 01:04:32,198
Now I know what I lost.

905
01:04:33,428 --> 01:04:36,168
I remember now. What do I do?

906
01:04:40,838 --> 01:04:42,438
What do I do?

907
01:05:13,868 --> 01:05:15,638
(Love on the Menu)

908
01:05:15,968 --> 01:05:18,368
I'm sorry for running away.

909
01:05:18,708 --> 01:05:21,278
I'm sorry for giving up on you.

910
01:05:21,438 --> 01:05:24,208
From now on, you and I are not a couple.

911
01:05:24,208 --> 01:05:27,478
If Seo Hyun runs away from home, will you take her in?

912
01:05:27,478 --> 01:05:29,418
You're fired now.

913
01:05:29,488 --> 01:05:31,118
Your meal ticket is gone.

914
01:05:31,118 --> 01:05:32,788
Give Han Gyu Oh to me.

915
01:05:32,858 --> 01:05:33,858
No way.

916
01:05:33,918 --> 01:05:35,988
Anyone else is fine, but not you.

917
01:05:35,988 --> 01:05:37,558
It's been a while, Gyu Rim.

918
01:05:37,858 --> 01:05:39,428
I'm sorry I haven't been in touch.

919
01:05:39,458 --> 01:05:43,368
I wasn't going to call, but I missed you so much.

920
01:05:43,368 --> 01:05:44,968
Do I look like a pushover to you?

